G4912.def:
συν-έχω 
[in LXX for עָצָר, חָבַר, etc. ;] 
__1. to hold together (τ. συνέχον τ. πάντα, Wis.1:7): of closing the ears, Actes 7:57 (τ. στόμα, Ésaïe 52:15); to hem in, press on every side: Luc 8:45 19:43. 
__2. to hold fast; 
__(a) of a prisoner, to hold in charge (Luc.; cf. exx. in Deiss., BS, 160; MM, xxiv): Luc 22:63; 
__(b) to constrain: 2 Corinthiens 5:14; pass., Luc 12:50, Actes 18:5 (τ. λόγῳ; cf. Field, Notes, 128), Philippiens 1:23; in pass., of ills, to be seized or afflicted by, suffering from: Matthieu 4:24, Luc 4:38 8:37, Actes 28:8.†

G4921.def:
συν-ίστημι 
[in LXX for צָוָה pi., קָהַל ni., etc.; 1Ma.12:43, 2Ma.4:24, 3Ma.1:19 (and frequently in these books) ;] 
__1. trans., 
__(a) to commend, recommend: with accusative of person(s), 2 Corinthiens 3:1 6:4 10:12 10:18; id. with dative, Romains 16:1 (as frequently at the beginning of a letter; Deiss., LAE, 226), 2 Corinthiens 5:12; before πρός, 2 Corinthiens 4:2; pass., before ὑπό, 2 Corinthiens 12:11; 
__(b) to show, prove, establish: with accusative, Romains 3:5 5:8, 2 Corinthiens 6:4; dupl. accusative, Galates 2:13; accusative and inf., 2 Corinthiens 7:11 
__2. Intrans., pf., συνέστηκα (as also 2 aor. and plpf.); 
__(a) to stand with or near: Luc 9:32; 
__(b) to be composed of, consist, cohere: Colossiens 1:17 (see Lft., in l), 2 Pierre 3:5.†

G4972.def:
σφραγίζω 
[in LXX chiefly for חָתַם (Deutéronome 32:34, al.), also for סָתַם (Da TH Daniel 8:26) ;] 
to seal, 
__(a) for security: Matthieu 27:66, Apocalypse 20:3; τ. καρπὸν τοῦτον, figuratively (cf. Deiss., BS, 238 f.; MM, xxiv; DB, iv, 427a), Romains 15:28; 
__(b) for concealment, hence, metaphorically, to hide (Da TH Daniel 9:24, Jean 14:17): Apocalypse 10:4 22:10; 
__(with) for distinction, Apocalypse 7:3-8; metaphorically, Éphésiens 4:30; mid., 2 Corinthiens 1:22; 
__(d) for authentication (Esther 8:8): Jean 3:33 6:27 (cf. κατα-σφραγίζω).†

G4988.def:
Σωσθένης, -ου, ὁ 
Sosthenes; 
__(a) a Jewish ruler: Actes 18:7; 
__(b) a Christian: 1 Corinthiens 1:1.†
